Description: on-demand backup companion for Timeshift
 Timeshift On Demand is a small GTK3 companion app for Timeshift
 (https://github.com/linuxmint/timeshift). It adds a manual on-demand
 backup trigger with live in-app progress, an at-a-glance snapshot and
 backup-drive status dashboard, and a cron-integrity watchdog for
 Timeshift's own scheduling — launched from a tray icon or desktop
 launcher. A login autostart entry and a resume-from-suspend hook can
 also prompt (zenity, with a live monitor window on confirmation) to run
 a backup, independent of whether the main window is open.
 .
 This package depends on the official timeshift package rather than
 bundling or forking it, and does not touch snapshot browsing, restore,
 or deletion — those remain Timeshift's own responsibility. Its three
 privileged actions (creating a snapshot, disabling a reappeared legacy
 cron file, and reading the snapshot list) are each authorized
 individually via polkit/pkexec; the application itself never runs as
 root.
